1
00:00:01,001 --> 00:00:03,003
(Yamanaka) I never expected a scout to come.

2
00:00:03,003 --> 00:00:06,740
This is an opportunity. It's a good opportunity for everyone to take revenge.

3
00:00:06,740 --> 00:00:08,742
What do you mean by quitting?

4
00:00:08,742 --> 00:00:13,580
Was Eternal Boys that light for Kakizaki? NOTE Eternal Boys

5
00:00:13,580 --> 00:00:20,287
♬～

6
00:00:20,287 --> 00:00:22,289
(Sanada) “Again”? NOTE Sanada Again

7
00:00:22,289 --> 00:00:26,693
(Fukuko) I brought you a present, yes.

8
00:00:26,693 --> 00:00:29,863
(Imagawa) It's a new song (Asai) Seriously?

9
00:00:29,863 --> 00:00:35,235
(Kakizaki) I'm actually timid and uncool.

10
00:00:35,235 --> 00:00:38,338
It can't be uncool, can it?

11
00:00:38,338 --> 00:00:41,041
Come to the last live, you too.

12
00:00:41,041 --> 00:00:43,043
I'll sing "Again"

13
00:01:03,497 --> 00:01:07,434
(Imagawa) It's tough! It's hard! Did you see the news? lotus

14
00:01:07,434 --> 00:01:09,870
(Lotus) Hehehehe hahahaha

15
00:01:09,870 --> 00:01:12,506
｟I'm quitting now｠

16
00:01:12,506 --> 00:01:14,508
I'm quitting my office

17
00:01:14,508 --> 00:01:16,510
Huh?

18
00:01:18,579 --> 00:01:24,384
♬～

19
00:01:24,384 --> 00:01:33,627
Has it already been decided? Yeah, it's a shame though

20
00:01:33,627 --> 00:01:38,632
I have just started consulting with a lawyer regarding bankruptcy proceedings.

21
00:01:40,934 --> 00:01:47,174
To be honest, I was barely managing my business with just Ren's earnings.

22
00:01:47,174 --> 00:01:51,512
(Imagawa) Then, are you going to stop Ren?

23
00:01:51,512 --> 00:01:55,349
I would rather move to a major company than stay here.

24
00:01:55,349 --> 00:01:57,951
I'm sure it's good

25
00:01:57,951 --> 00:02:01,355
I want to support this great opportunity.

26
00:02:01,355 --> 00:02:03,991
(Imagawa) Yes, but...

27
00:02:03,991 --> 00:02:10,998
That's why Manpuku Entertainment is over and Eternal Shonen has disbanded.

28
00:02:12,566 --> 00:02:17,271
I have no choice but to cancel the live concert I had planned.

29
00:02:20,574 --> 00:02:25,012
Everyone, please find a new job as soon as possible.

30
00:02:28,615 --> 00:02:31,685
(Ishida) I don't like it.

31
00:02:31,685 --> 00:02:33,687
Isn't it okay? please

32
00:02:33,687 --> 00:02:36,657
I don't want to give up. I don't want to give up either.

33
00:02:36,657 --> 00:02:38,959
please

34
00:02:50,771 --> 00:02:55,776
I'm really sorry

35
00:03:00,881 --> 00:03:06,820
There's nothing I can do now

36
00:03:28,909 --> 00:03:48,695
♬～

37
00:03:48,695 --> 00:03:53,600
Are you really giving up this easily?

38
00:03:53,600 --> 00:03:55,602
ah?

39
00:03:55,602 --> 00:04:00,974
No. Isn't it so easy to find the next one?

40
00:04:00,974 --> 00:04:04,978
I guess it can't be helped...

41
00:04:06,513 --> 00:04:11,885
The old man has gotten better at not giving up.

42
00:04:11,885 --> 00:04:13,887
I don't like it

43
00:04:19,793 --> 00:04:25,199
I don't want to give up yet

44
00:04:25,199 --> 00:04:30,070
♬～

45
00:04:30,070 --> 00:04:34,074
(Sound of door opening and closing)

46
00:04:35,175 --> 00:04:37,177
(sigh)

47
00:04:38,178 --> 00:04:40,180
(Ishida) He's not coming, everyone.

48
00:04:43,684 --> 00:04:48,121
(Imagawa) I guess we should start first.

49
00:04:48,121 --> 00:04:50,123
(Ishida) After all, I'm going home too.

50
00:04:50,123 --> 00:04:52,659
I will resume my part-time job at the cram school tomorrow.

51
00:04:52,659 --> 00:04:57,431
Eh... (Ishida) Then go first.

52
00:04:57,431 --> 00:04:59,433
Hey…

53
00:05:05,439 --> 00:05:10,711
Well, let's practice just the two of us.

54
00:05:10,711 --> 00:05:13,046
(Imagawa) Ah

55
00:05:13,046 --> 00:05:16,316
Come to think of it, Mr. Imagawa, today is the day of distribution, right?

56
00:05:17,951 --> 00:05:21,021
What are you doing?

57
00:05:21,021 --> 00:05:25,926
Ah... sorry

58
00:05:25,926 --> 00:05:30,397
I have some business to do this evening.

59
00:05:30,397 --> 00:05:32,399
What? Business?

60
00:05:34,902 --> 00:05:39,806
Does someone you know want to join a theater company? That's it

61
00:05:42,342 --> 00:05:47,648
So what about Eternal Boy?

62
00:05:49,483 --> 00:05:55,822
No, I want to continue.

63
00:05:55,822 --> 00:06:01,595
As expected, there's nothing I can do this time.

64
00:06:07,000 --> 00:06:09,002
sorry…

65
00:06:17,311 --> 00:06:21,281
(Asai) Actually, I'll be at Kaoru's school starting next week.

66
00:06:21,281 --> 00:06:30,691
I'm a soccer school teacher, so I don't have a part-time job anymore...

67
00:06:30,691 --> 00:06:35,162
That's good (Asai) I'm sorry.

68
00:06:40,367 --> 00:06:47,007
I guess I'm going back to being a regular host now, too?

69
00:07:03,457 --> 00:07:07,861
Ah, what are you going to do about today's broadcast? What?

70
00:07:07,861 --> 00:07:13,534
Eh, it's broadcasting. Today's duty is me and Mr. Yamanaka.

71
00:07:13,534 --> 00:07:16,436
Are you still doing it?

72
00:07:16,436 --> 00:07:20,474
Sanada: Have you found a new job?

73
00:07:20,474 --> 00:07:24,111
No... Are you looking for it properly?

74
00:07:25,812 --> 00:07:28,849
If that's the case, I'll ask President Fukuko to do it.

75
00:07:28,849 --> 00:07:31,151
I am also being introduced by the president...

76
00:07:32,319 --> 00:07:34,321
Why…

77
00:07:38,592 --> 00:07:41,628
Why do people give up so easily?

78
00:07:45,499 --> 00:07:48,836
It can't be helped, but...

79
00:07:50,804 --> 00:07:52,806
but…

80
00:07:55,008 --> 00:07:57,010
nevertheless…

81
00:07:59,346 --> 00:08:01,348
bad

82
00:08:01,348 --> 00:08:14,595
♬～

83
00:08:14,595 --> 00:08:18,565
♬ (Child) If you are happy, clap your hands (clap)

84
00:08:18,565 --> 00:08:21,668
Dad can sing too.

85
00:08:21,668 --> 00:08:23,670
Then let's go together...

86
00:08:23,670 --> 00:08:30,377
♬ (2 people) If you are happy, clap your hands (clap)

87
00:08:30,377 --> 00:08:33,881
♬(2 people) If we're happy, we'll show it with our attitude.

88
00:08:33,881 --> 00:08:37,284
♬Come on, let's all clap our hands

89
00:08:43,657 --> 00:08:46,393
Sanada's trouble consultation room!

90
00:08:46,393 --> 00:08:49,029
(applause)

91
00:08:49,029 --> 00:08:51,665
Today I received messages from everyone.

92
00:08:51,665 --> 00:08:53,834
I will answer your concerns

93
00:08:53,834 --> 00:08:57,237
So without further ado...

94
00:08:57,237 --> 00:09:01,642
"It's hard to be told at work that this is a job that anyone can do."

95
00:09:01,642 --> 00:09:05,212
"What would you do, Sanada-san?"

96
00:09:05,212 --> 00:09:12,986
Hmm... then you should try it.

97
00:09:12,986 --> 00:09:15,689
I wish I could say it, but at times like this

98
00:09:15,689 --> 00:09:19,026
Actually, I can't say it.

99
00:09:19,026 --> 00:09:22,029
I was often told that too.

100
00:09:23,263 --> 00:09:27,901
But I'm sure somewhere

101
00:09:27,901 --> 00:09:31,371
There are people who understand you

102
00:09:31,371 --> 00:09:35,242
We just haven't met yet

103
00:09:35,242 --> 00:09:41,248
I'm sure there will be an encounter that will reward everything I've done up until now.

104
00:09:41,248 --> 00:09:43,750
Everyone has one too.

105
00:09:51,959 --> 00:09:55,162
Thank you for your comment

106
00:10:08,942 --> 00:10:12,579
Sorry I'm alone

107
00:10:19,887 --> 00:10:28,262
No, that's right, I can't do it alone.

108
00:10:28,262 --> 00:10:33,634
There must be six eternal boys.

109
00:10:37,070 --> 00:10:40,007
(sob)

110
00:10:40,007 --> 00:10:42,442
sorry

111
00:10:42,442 --> 00:10:47,814
I feel like who benefits from the old man's tears?

112
00:10:55,355 --> 00:11:05,999
I don't even want to be an idol, I can become one.

113
00:11:05,999 --> 00:11:09,937
I've never thought about it

114
00:11:09,937 --> 00:11:17,945
Just go back to how it was before

115
00:11:19,012 --> 00:11:25,018
But still...

116
00:11:30,691 --> 00:11:34,094
I don't want to break up

117
00:11:34,094 --> 00:11:39,333
Still more...

118
00:11:44,538 --> 00:11:49,610
I want to be an idol with everyone

119
00:11:52,279 --> 00:11:57,117
(sob)

120
00:11:57,117 --> 00:12:00,020
I have to be a forever boy.

121
00:12:00,020 --> 00:12:02,756
I don't want to give up yet

122
00:12:02,756 --> 00:12:05,993
(Kakizaki) Let's do it live. I want to sing "Again" with everyone.
